# BlockML Libraries & Versioning

## Recommended BML namespace

Prefer a `bml` package segment after the domain so BML FQNs stay distinct from companion FQNs:

```text
<domain>.bml.*     e.g. org.blockml.bml.* · com.example.bml.*
```

This is a recommendation, not a requirement. Physical paths still mirror FQNs: `blocks/org/blockml/bml/core/Block.bml` → `org.blockml.bml.core.Block`.

## Library structure

- Abstract base type: `org.blockml.bml.core.BlockLibrary` in `node_modules/@blockml/core/blocks/org/blockml/bml/core/BlockLibrary.bml`
- Framework base type — **not** exported via any Library `blocks`
- Concrete libraries: `<name>Library</name>`, filename **`Library.bml`**, `baseType="bcore:BlockLibrary"`
- FQN = `{package}.Library` from the file's package path
- **Membership is location-based** — a Block belongs to the nearest `Library.bml` at the same package level or above. Search stops one level below the source folder (`srcDir`). Nested libraries are allowed; the first Library found walking up wins.
- Catalog members (`description`, `language`, `readMe`, `bootstrap`, `dependencies`, `subLibraries`, `schemas`) are **public** and **`readOnly`**. Authored `blocks` lists are not membership SSOT.

## Nested libraries

Multiple `Library.bml` files may exist at different package levels (e.g. `org.blockml.bml.Library` + `org.blockml.bml.compiler.Library`). The nearest Library walking up from a Block owns it.

```text
Typical:  inner dependencies → outer Library
```

## Effective block version

```text
effectiveBlockVersion =
  own <version>       if present
  else library.version if a nearest Library.bml owns the block
  else unversioned
```

- **Framework blocks** (`org.blockml.bml.*`): version only on `Library.bml`
- Third-party libraries use the same effectiveBlockVersion rule; no other namespace is exempted
- **Block in library** with own `<version>`: must be `>= library.version`
- **Standalone block**: `<version>` optional; omitted means unversioned
- `bml:version` on a reference to an unversioned type → `BML_UNKNOWN_VERSION`

## Instance references (`bml:version`)

- **Optional** on external references and Library TypeReferenceEntity sugar (`dependencies`,
  `subLibraries`, `readFirst`, `bootstrap`, `language`) — omitted = resolve from
  TypeRegistry / library context
- **Present** = exact-version assert against the **referenced** type's effective version (`value` for sugar) →
  `BML_UNKNOWN_VERSION` if no match or the type is unversioned
- Example dependency pin: `<blockml:Library bml:version="3.0.0" />`
- Authored `blocks` lists (if present on BlockLibrary) are ignored for membership

## Library file pattern

```xml
<name>Library</name>
<baseType>bcore:BlockLibrary</baseType>
<version>3.0.0</version>
<dependencies>
  <composition><blockml:Library bml:version="3.0.0" /></composition>
</dependencies>
```
